{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/unitsbydimension"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/WorkingWithQuantity","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/StoringAndEncodingQuantities","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Looking Up Units by Dimension","role":"article"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitsByDimension","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every unit in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"text":" is defined twice: once as a flat, ready-made value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"Units.cup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Units.newton","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and once under a namespace named after its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dimension (","type":"text"},{"code":"Units.Volume.cup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Units.Weight.newton","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). The namespaces give you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a way to see, enumerate, and pick from just one dimension.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"The dimension namespaces","type":"heading","anchor":"The-dimension-namespaces","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated namespaces mirror the framework’s dimensions:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Namespace","type":